===================

1. Scope

This license applies to the copyright-protected portions of BrightTerm
that Dany Kim (the “Licensor”) provides under this license
(the “Software”). Conditions concerning copies and modified copies
apply to source and executable forms and to distributions containing
those protected portions.

Third-party components remain subject to their respective licenses.
This license does not revoke or restrict MIT permissions for copies
of BrightTerm previously provided under the MIT License.

2. Permitted activities

Subject to these conditions, everyone is granted a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, run, reproduce, modify,
and redistribute the Software free of charge.

Personal use and internal use by businesses and organizations are
permitted. Using the Software as a tool to perform paid work is also
permitted. Paid provision of the Software described in section 3
is not permitted.

This license does not itself require disclosure of the source code
of modified copies.

3. Prohibited paid provision

Without separate written permission from the Licensor, you may not:

(a) sell, rent, or redistribute copies or modified copies of the
    Software for payment;
(b) condition receipt of a copy, or permission to install or run
    that copy, on payment or other consideration; or
(c) supply copies of the Software to third parties as part of a
    paid software, hardware, subscription, or service package.

Listing the Software at a separate price of zero, or changing its
name or logo, does not avoid these restrictions.

Charges for training or support supplied independently of obtaining
copies or permission to use the Software are not prohibited by
themselves. Merely using the Software as a work tool does not make
the resulting work or service a paid bundle. Voluntary donations
or advertising revenue alone do not turn free distribution into
paid provision.

4. Redistribution conditions

When redistributing, you must:

(a) provide this license and applicable copyright notices;
(b) preserve required third-party licenses and notices;
(c) identify modified copies as modified and not misrepresent
    them as official distributions made or approved by the Licensor;
    and
(d) for distributions with an interactive graphical user interface,
    make the following original copyright notice accessible through
    an About or Legal Notices screen:
    “BrightTerm original portions:
     Copyright (c) 2026 Dany Kim”

Modifiers may add copyright notices for their own modifications.

5. Names and logos

This license does not grant a general trademark license to the
BrightTerm name or logos. It does not exclude required copyright
notices, truthful statements of origin, or uses permitted by law.
TRADEMARKS.md provides guidance on identifying official and modified
distributions.

6. Separate permission

The Licensor may authorize activities described in section 3 or
other activities through a separate written agreement. Such
permission applies only to the parties and scope of that agreement
and does not authorize others to violate this license.

7. Violations and termination

No permission is granted in the first place for paid provision
that this license does not permit.

Your rights under this license terminate automatically if you
violate its conditions. Reinstatement requires written confirmation
from the Licensor. Termination does not discharge liability already
incurred.

This section does not terminate existing MIT permissions,
third-party licenses, or rights independently recognized by law.
A distributor's violation alone does not terminate an otherwise
lawful recipient's independent license.

8. Warranty, liability, and interpretation

To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Software is provided
“AS IS”, without warranties. Except for liability that cannot
lawfully be excluded, the Licensor is not liable for damages
arising from use of the Software.

This license is interpreted under the laws of the Republic of
Korea without displacing applicable mandatory law. The Korean
text controls if the Korean and English texts differ.
